# Sample API requests (Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code REST Client).
# Replace @requestId with a real id (e.g. from GET /api/requests), and @version with its version.
@host = http://localhost:5000
@requestId = 000000000000000000000000
@version = 0

### Liveness + Mongo connection
GET {{host}}/api/health

### Recreate the test data: delete + 100,000 requests (Development only)
POST {{host}}/api/seed?count=100000&reset=true

### First page, default sort (createdAt desc)
GET {{host}}/api/requests?page=1&pageSize=25

### Combined filtering + sorting
GET {{host}}/api/requests?status=Completed&priority=High&sortBy=priority&sortDirection=Asc&pageSize=10

### Text search (whole words) in title and organization name
GET {{host}}/api/requests?search=urgent

### Date range
GET {{host}}/api/requests?createdFrom=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&createdTo=2026-06-30T23:59:59Z

### Summary (aggregations, served from the cache)
GET {{host}}/api/requests/summary

### A single request
GET {{host}}/api/requests/{{requestId}}

### Status update with optimistic concurrency (a second send with the same version -> 409)
PATCH {{host}}/api/requests/{{requestId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "InProgress", "expectedVersion": {{version}}, "changedBy": "dana" }

### Unknown status -> 400 with the list of allowed values
PATCH {{host}}/api/requests/{{requestId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "newStatus": "Foo", "expectedVersion": 0 }

### Status-change history
GET {{host}}/api/requests/{{requestId}}/history

### Bulk update (partial success)
PATCH {{host}}/api/requests/bulk-status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newStatus": "Waiting",
  "changedBy": "dana",
  "items": [
    { "id": "{{requestId}}", "expectedVersion": {{version}} },
    { "id": "000000000000000000000001", "expectedVersion": 0 }
  ]
}
